  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The face diagonals of a rectangular prism are measured to be 7, 8 and 9 units. Find the length of the space diagonal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sqrt{97}$ units.\n\nAdd the three face-diagonal equations and divide by two.",
      "worked": "Let the edge lengths be $a$, $b$ and $c$, and the space diagonal be $d$.\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2+b^2&=7^2\\\\a^2+c^2&=8^2\\\\b^2+c^2&=9^2\\\\2(a^2+b^2+c^2)&=49+64+81\\\\2(a^2+b^2+c^2)&=194\\\\a^2+b^2+c^2&=97\\\\d^2&=97\\\\d&=\\sqrt{97}\\text{ units}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
